  "worked_solution": "Notice that the $3$rd row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (3\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-12\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-12(10-6) \\\\  & =(-12)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
